“I told you,” I said, not meaning to sound so angry. “I’m thirsty.”
“Gabe, really.” She glanced at Dad, then went back to staring at the
pyramid.
“Dad, do you think Uncle Ben can take us inside the pyramid?” I
asked enthusiastically. “That would really be outstanding.”
