The next day, Sunday, it rained. I was very disappointed.
My brother, Kevin, stood beside me at the window, watching the
raindrops patter against the glass. He was very disappointed, too. He and
his friends had planned to finish their Mud Monsters video in the woods.
“Today we were going to tape the big finish where the Mud Monsters
rise up out of the mud,” he said.
“Maybe the rain will stop,” I told him.
“It doesn’t matter,” Kevin sighed. “We won’t be able to shoot
anyway.”
“Why not?” I asked.
“Too muddy,” he replied.
