Clay covered his head with his hands. All three of us raised our eyes to the
trees.
Were there really snakes up there?
It was too dark to see anything. The leaves were so thick, no sunlight
filtered through.
Suddenly, I heard a gentle hissing sound.
At first I thought it was just the rustle of the leaves.
But then the hissing grew louder—until all of the trees seemed to be hissing
down at us.
“Run!” I cried.
