“The path goes right through the barn to the other side,” Luke called to me.
“Come on, Lizzy!” He motioned for me to join them.
I spotted a small sign painted to the right of the barn’s double doors. It read:
BAT BARN.
“Hey—are there bats in there?” I called, feeling a cold shudder run down
my back. I like most animals. But bats really give me the creeps.
Luke stepped inside the barn. Clay hung back, standing just outside the
