She raised the script and shook it furiously.
“The pages of my script—they’ve all been glued together!” she fumed.
Startled gasps rose up around the stage.
“That’s it!” Ms. Walker cried. She heaved the script at the wall. “That was
the last joke! The play is canceled! Everybody go home! It’s canceled!”
