I shivered.
Turning to leave, a memory flashed through my mind.
The INSTA-TAN bottle. We hadn’t dropped it back into the Dumpster.
We had tossed it into the woods on the other side of the neighbors’ house.
“Yes!” I cried happily. “Yes!”
We had chased each other across the neighbors’ yard—and I’d heaved
