excited barking of the dogs in the distance. “Now what?”
The bottle was shattered into a dozen pieces. My evidence was gone. I
had nothing to show Dr. Murkin. Nothing at all.
With an angry cry, I tossed the piece of glass at the trees. Then I
wearily slunk toward home.
Mom and Dad hurried to a school meeting after dinner. I went upstairs to
