I stopped with a gasp when I realized Marissa wasn’t there.
I was alone.
Alone in the middle of the forest.
“Marissa—?” I called, feeling the panic tighten my chest. Where was
she?
Where was I?
“Marissa—? Marissa—?”
15
“Marissa—?”
